    "chunk_size_bytes": 759,
    "chunk_text": "Gold prices surge in Sri Lanka\n\nColombo, June 15 (Daily Mirror) - Gold prices in Sri Lanka have risen sharply following a significant increase in global gold rates, which have climbed to around USD 4,325 in international markets.\n\nAs a result, local gold prices have increased by approximately Rs. 6,000 compared to rates recorded at 9.00 a.m. today (15), traders said.\n\nIn the Colombo Sea Street gold market, the price of a 22-carat gold sovereign was recorded at Rs. 360,600 this morning.\n\nMeanwhile, the price of a 24-carat gold sovereign, which stood at Rs. 386,000 on Saturday (June 13), has risen to Rs. 392,000 today, reflecting the upward trend in global bullion prices.\n\nGold Price Today in Sri Lanka \u2013 22K & 24K Rates, Trends, and Investment Guide"
  },
