    "chunk_text": "Former Southern Province CM\u2019s Secretary arrested in Rs. 16.5 Mn corruption probe\n\nColombo, June 15 (Daily Mirror) - A private secretary to former Southern Province Chief Minister Shan Wijayalal De Silva was arrested by the Commission to Investigate Allegations of Bribery or Corruption over allegations of causing a financial loss of Rs. 16.5 million to the State through a procurement-related corruption offense.\n\nAccording to CIABOC, the suspect is accused of bypassing established procurement procedures while serving under the Southern Province Chief Ministry to facilitate the selection of a particular manufacturing company for the supply of chairs intended for public volunteer societies, thereby granting an undue advantage to the supplier.\n\nInvestigations revealed that 16,361 chairs purchased through the Southern Province Development Authority were subsequently transported and delivered to the residences or offices of 54 Provincial Council members across the Southern Province\u2019s three districts.\n\nThe Bribery Commission stated that the irregular procurement process resulted in a loss of Rs. 16.5 million to the government.\n\nThe suspect is due to be produced before the Colombo Chief Magistrate\u2019s Court for further proceedings."
