    "chunk_text": "\u201870s Pop Hits & Baila\u2019\n\nAfter his recent trip to England where he was originally scheduled to do three shows but ended doing seven, Ravi Sebastian is in the news again.\n\nYes, he is in great demand, overseas, and will be off to Dubai, next month, to create the \u201970s pop hits scene and baila.\n\nThe show is scheduled for Saturday, 25th July, at the Mercure Hotel Dubai Barsha Heights, from 8.00 pm to 3.00 am.\n\nProviding the music for Rajiv to do the needful is the band Seven Notes, said to be a very popular and much in demand in that region.\n\nThe organizer of this event, \u201870s Pop Hits & Baila,\u2019 is Niluk Uswaththa who booms away on bass for Seven Notes.\n\nIn fact, Niluk, and his wife Apeksha who, incidentally, was featured in Glam Scene in last Thursday\u2019s The Island newspaper, were in Sri Lanka last month.\n\nThe Sri Lankans in Dubai, I\u2019m told, are eagerly looking forward to having Rajiv in their midst as they know, for sure, it\u2019s going to be a night to remember.\n\nIn London, Rajiv\u2019s seven events are still the talk of the town among the Sri Lankans who took in the action.\n\nLeave a Reply Cancel replyYour email address will not be published. Required fields are marked *Comment * Name *\n\nSave my name, email, and website in this browser for the next time I comment."
