    "chunk_text": "Stock market benchmark index rises in the wake of M-E peace deal news\n\nAt the time of closure yesterday the CSE benchmark index rose 3.43 percent following news of a US-Iran peace deal, brokers said.\n\n\u2018The positive sentiment was seen across all sectors due to the peace deal between the US and Iran and also the oil price dropped in the world market, market analysts said.\n\nThe All Share Price Index rose 743.22 points to close at 22,380; while the S&P SL20 rose 3.28 percent, or 197.47 points, at 6,224.\n\nThe top seven crossings were: Amana Takaful 7.5 million shares crossed to the tune of Rs 173 million and its shares traded at Rs 23, Asiri Surgical Hospitals 9.2 million shares crossed to the tune of Rs 169 million; its shares traded at Rs 18.50, HNB 250,000 shares crossed for Rs 101 million and its shares sold at Rs 404.\n\nAitken Spence 190,000 shares crossed to the tune of Rs 98 million; its shares traded at Rs 143, Distilleries 1.7 million shares crossed to the tune of Rs 97 million; its shares traded at Rs 57.50, Ceylon Land Equity 4.4 million shares crossed for Rs 46 million; its shares sold at Rs 10.50 and JKH two million shares crossed for Rs 41 million; its shares sold at Rs 20.40.\n\nIn the retail market companies that mainly contributed to the turnover were; Asiri Surgical Rs 274 million (15 million shares traded), Prime Lands Residencies Rs 198 million (4.2 million shares traded),Commercial Bank Rs 147 million(700,000 shares traded) Access Engineering Rs 132 million (1.7 million shares traded), Softlogic Capital Rs 109 million (7.7 million shares traded), CCS Rs 80 million (550,000 shares traded) and JKH Rs 74 million (3.6 million shares traded). During the day 206 million share volumes changed hands in 34511 transactions.\n\nBanking sector counters, especially Amana Takaful, HNB and Commercial Bank performed well while in the manufacturing sector, especially JKH, also actively participated."
