    "chunk_text": "CanCham to launch dialogue on women\u2019s economic empowerment and SME growth\n\nThe Canadian Chamber of Commerce in Sri Lanka (CanCham Sri Lanka) will convene a high-level dialogue on strengthening women\u2019s development, economic empowerment and women-led Small and Medium Enterprises (SMEs) on June 17 at CanCham House in Colombo.\n\nThe initiative reflects the Chamber\u2019s growing commitment to promoting inclusive economic growth by enhancing opportunities for women entrepreneurs and business leaders across Sri Lanka and the wider Indo-Pacific region.\n\nThe dialogue will feature Dr. Hina Shah, Founder of the International Centre for Entrepreneurship and Career Development (ICECD), an internationally acclaimed institution that has empowered thousands of women through entrepreneurship development, livelihood creation, skills enhancement and economic empowerment programmes.\n\nCanCham Sri Lanka said women\u2019s development remains a strategic priority for the Chamber, noting that stronger participation of women in the economy is essential for innovation, employment generation, poverty reduction and sustainable national development.\n\nThe event will also mark the launch of a new Chamber-led initiative aimed at fostering closer collaboration among stakeholders committed to advancing women\u2019s entrepreneurship and supporting women-led enterprises.\n\nAccording to organisers, the dialogue will review achievements, challenges and progress made in women\u2019s economic empowerment in Sri Lanka while identifying practical measures to strengthen women\u2019s participation in business and economic development.\n\nKey discussions will focus on promoting the growth and competitiveness of women-led SMEs, facilitating networking and knowledge sharing among entrepreneurs from Sri Lanka, India, Canada and other Indo-Pacific countries, and building strategic partnerships involving the private sector, government agencies, development organisations, financial institutions and international stakeholders."
