    "md5": "bcf18ca20c9e9f38dafd0cb265897341",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1757,
    "chunk_text": "Companies involved in the pilot phase of the project include 99x, hSenid, ADA, Virtusa, Sysco LABS, Fortude, Covalent Systems, and IIBA, with representatives from several of these organisations attending the event as well. SLASSCOM also acknowledged the support extended by leading universities that came on board as pilot partners and demonstrated openness towards exploring and piloting this initiative.\n\nSpeaking at the launch, SLASSCOM Chairperson Shehani Senevirathne stated,\u201cThe SLASSCOM Internship Platform is a timely and important initiative that addresses a critical challenge faced by both students and universities today. By enabling structured, industry-aligned virtual internships, we are creating more equitable access to practical learning opportunities while strengthening collaboration between academia and industry. This initiative reflects SLASSCOM\u2019s continued commitment to developing future-ready digital talent and supporting the long-term growth of Sri Lanka\u2019s IT and BPM industry.\u201d\n\nSLASSCOM Director - Operations Bimal Gunapala stated, \u201cShrinking physical placements at reputed companies have put universities under intense pressure to make internships optional. While this allows students to graduate on time, it threatens to further widen an already existing employability skill gap. Our virtual platform is a critical intervention\u2014connecting students with real companies, real supervisors, and real projects. By keeping industry doors open digitally, we preserve the vital, hands-on experience our workforce demands.\u201d\n\nThe launch also highlighted the platform\u2019s potential to promote equitable access to meaningful internships and strengthen the long-term sustainability of Sri Lanka\u2019s digital talent ecosystem."
